NCMAT v7
#
# Test file with an unusual VDOS, not intended for physics usage.
#
# Provenance:
#
#   The file H2_liquid.ncmat from the Liquids plugin by D. DiJulio and J. I.
#   Marquez Damian (https://github.com/dddijulio/ncrystal-plugin-Liquids,
#   commit 308f623). Only the VDOS was kept, written with up to 7 significant
#   digits.
#
# Why it is a test case:
#
#   A smooth VDOS where all weight is at very low energies (below 0.055eV,
#   with a mean single phonon energy of 5meV), for the lightest atom. The
#   phonon expansion therefore needs a very large number of orders, which used
#   to give kernels with reduced energy range at all temperatures, and
#   failures at room temperature.
#
@DENSITY
  0.071 g_per_cm3
@DYNINFO
  element  H
  fraction 1
  type     vdos
  vdos_egrid .00013786 .055144062
